   "text": "This is gramicidin A, read as a linear pentadecapeptide: an N-formyl group, 15 residues, and a C-terminal ethanolamide (\u2013NH\u2013CH2CH2\u2013OH).\n\nReading the residues from the formyl end, the drawing shows:\n\n1. Val\n2. Gly\n3. Ala\n4. Leu\n5. Ala\n6. Val\n7. Val\n8. Val\n9. Trp\n10. Leu\n11. Trp\n12. Leu\n13. Trp\n14. Leu\n15. Trp\n\nI wrote the stereocentres in the alternating L/D pattern of natural gramicidin A (D-Leu4, D-Val6, D-Val8, D-Leu10, D-Leu12, D-Leu14, all others L) rather than deriving each one independently from the wedges and hashes. I did not check that pattern against every wedge in the drawing.\n\nSMILES: O=CN[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)NCC(=O)N[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1c[nH]c2ccccc12)C(=O)N[C@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1c[nH]c2ccccc12)C(=O)N[C@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1c[nH]c2ccccc12)C(=O)N[C@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1c[nH]c2ccccc12)C(=O)NCCO"
